Logos shown on the installer's credits page.

Each is the project's own mark, taken from the project's own hands rather
than from a clip-art site, and used to credit them. None of these projects
endorses SakuraOS, and none of these marks is ours. If any of them would
rather we did not use theirs, remove the entry -- the credit can be text.

  assets/credit-kde.svg       KDE, from kde.org brand assets
  assets/credit-limine.png    Limine, from the Limine repository
  assets/credit-cachyos.svg   CachyOS, from cachyos.org
  assets/credit-systemd.svg   systemd, from systemd/systemd docs/assets
  assets/credit-linux.svg     Tux, the Linux mascot, originally by Larry Ewing
                              (lewing@isc.tamu.edu), created with GIMP
  assets/credit-gnu.png       The GNU head, from Wikimedia Commons

Arch Linux's logo is not bundled. It is read at runtime from
/usr/share/pixmaps/archlinux-logo.svg, which the filesystem package provides,
so it always matches the machine it is shown on.

The Linux mascot carries the customary request that Larry Ewing be credited
as its author; that is the reason his name is written here rather than only
in a commit message.
  assets/credit-flatpak.png   Flatpak, from the flatpak/flatpak repository
